 <apex:pageBlock id="page8" mode="edit">

           <p class="s38" style="padding-bottom: 5pt;margin-left: 5pt;margin-right: 5pt;text-indent: 0pt;text-align: justify;">Retiring federal employees under both the CSRS and FERS retirement systems have the opportunity to ensure the continuation of benefits to survivors with an insurable interest. A person with an insurable interest is an insurance term, applying to a person who would benefit financially by your continuing to be alive. Such persons would include, but are not limited to a widow, widower, former spouse, and children.</p>
             
           <p class="s38" style="padding-bottom: 5pt;margin-left: 5pt;margin-right: 5pt;text-indent: 0pt;text-align: center;font-size: 14pt;color: #2E5395;"><b>CSRS Employees</b></p>
             
           <p class="s38" style="padding-bottom: 3pt;margin-left: 5pt;margin-right: 5pt;text-indent: 0pt;text-align: center;">
                        <span class="s38" style="color: red;">• 
                               </span>
                                 May elect a Survivor Benefit up to 55% of their retirement annuity or as little as $1.00.</p>

   
        <p class="s38" style="padding-bottom: 3pt;margin-left: 5pt;margin-right: 5pt;text-indent: 0pt;text-align: center;">
                        <span class="s38" style="color: red;">• 
                               </span>
                                   Retirement annuity will be reduced depending on the benefit elected.</p>
  
    
        <p class="s38" style="padding-bottom: 3pt;margin-left: 5pt;margin-right: 5pt;text-indent: 0pt;text-align: center;">
                        <span class="s38" style="color: red;">• 
                               </span>
                                   Cost of first $3,600 (annually) is 2.5% or $90.00.</p>
   
    
        <p class="s38" style="padding-bottom: 15pt;margin-left: 5pt;margin-right: 5pt;text-indent: 0pt;text-align: center;">
                        <span class="s38" style="color: red;">• 
                               </span>
                                   Plus 10% of any amount over $3,600 used as a base</p>
        
        <p class="s38" style="padding-bottom: 5pt;margin-left: 5pt;margin-right: 5pt;text-indent: 0pt;text-align: justify;">To provide a full survivor benefit for your current or former spouse, your annual annuity will be reduced by 2.5 percent of the first $3,600 = $90.00 plus 10 percent of the annuity over $3,600.</p>
        <p style="text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;">
            <br/>
            </p>
